    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d406">

                <pb facs="0738" n="634" xml:id="pg634"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President’s Special Assistant</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President,
                        and the President’s Reply</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d406-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-12-01">December 1, 1943</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. President</hi>: What do you think of letting the
                    Russians give dinner tonight—your last chance at Russian food</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>OK but I have to leave <hi rendition="#italic">early</hi> as we sleep at the
                        camp.</p>
                    <closer><signed>FDR</signed></closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d406-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d406-f1-content">
                <p>According to Sherwood, p. 796, these messages were exchanged near the end of the
                    tripartite luncheon meeting of December 1, 1943 (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg585">p. 585</ref>). For a facsimile reproduction
                    of the messages, which were handwritten, see Sherwood, p. 797.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
